{'page_ID': 7, 'quote_ID': 1, 'quote_text': '“If I had a flower for every time I thought of you...I could walk through my garden forever.”', 'quote_author': 'Alfred Tennyson', 'quote_tags': ['friendship', 'love']}
{'page_ID': 7, 'quote_ID': 2, 'quote_text': '“Some people never go crazy. What truly horrible lives they must lead.”', 'quote_author': 'Charles Bukowski', 'quote_tags': ['humor']}
{'page_ID': 7, 'quote_ID': 3, 'quote_text': '“The trouble with having an open mind, of course, is that people will insist on coming along and trying to put things in it.”', 'quote_author': 'Terry Pratchett', 'quote_tags': ['humor', 'open-mind', 'thinking']}
{'page_ID': 7, 'quote_ID': 4, 'quote_text': '“Think left and think right and think low and think high. Oh, the thinks you can think up if only you try!”', 'quote_author': 'Dr. Seuss', 'quote_tags': ['humor', 'philosophy']}
{'page_ID': 7, 'quote_ID': 5, 'quote_text': "“What really knocks me out is a book that, when you're all done reading it, you wish the author that wrote it was a terrific friend of yours and you could call him up on the phone whenever you felt like it. That doesn't happen much, though.”", 'quote_author': 'J.D. Salinger', 'quote_tags': ['authors', 'books', 'literature', 'reading', 'writing']}
{'page_ID': 7, 'quote_ID': 6, 'quote_text': '“The reason I talk to myself is because I’m the only one whose answers I accept.”', 'quote_author': 'George Carlin', 'quote_tags': ['humor', 'insanity', 'lies', 'lying', 'self-indulgence', 'truth']}
